## ROLE AND OVERALL OBJECTIVE

Act as an expert full-stack software engineer, senior UI/UX designer, product designer, database architect, cybersecurity specialist, AI integration engineer, accessibility specialist, and quality assurance engineer.

Your task is to design, develop, test, and document **AquaTrack**, a complete, modern, interactive, visually stunning, secure, and genuinely functional water conservation and environmental education web application.

Build the entire project from scratch in an empty project folder. There is no existing application to modify. Initialize the project, install and configure dependencies, create the complete directory structure, implement every required frontend and backend component, establish the database, configure authentication, and build the actual working application.

Do not simply produce a design concept, a landing page, a static prototype, a collection of disconnected components, or a dashboard filled with fabricated information. The result must be a cohesive, usable, full-stack application in which the features, buttons, forms, charts, navigation, settings, games, authentication, and data operations genuinely work.

Every requirement below is part of the project specification. Do not silently omit features, shorten the language list, replace functional features with placeholders, or treat requested functionality as optional merely because implementation is extensive.

When a feature requires an external service, API key, database, OAuth configuration, browser permission, or other dependency, implement the integration properly and document the setup. Where a service cannot function without configuration, provide a clear and honest unavailable state instead of pretending it is working.

